# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 137-142 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 14 — CHAPTER 16, LEAN, 2026-09-23): the feast of weeks without a harvest, the hand's measure
# (137), the rejoicing by analogy, the household's precedence, the three commandments of the pilgrimage (138), "these statutes" — the assembly's laws and the
# feasts' (139), the booth for yourself, the old booth, the companion's booth, the eight days, the threshing floor and the winepress (140), the rejoicing's
# offerings (141), seven days of compensation, the blessing, "only" joyful — the nights (142). Every row read whole; the cuts by consonants (ch16_ink.SP_).
from ch16_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(137, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL MAKE THE FEAST OF WEEKS TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" (16:10) — SINCE IT SAYS "THE FEAST OF HARVEST, THE FIRSTFRUITS OF YOUR WORK" (EXODUS 23:16), MIGHT IT BE THAT IF YOU HAVE A HARVEST YOU KEEP THE FESTIVAL AND IF NOT, NOT? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL MAKE THE FEAST OF WEEKS" — WITH A HARVEST OR WITHOUT. The head row of piska 137 ({SP_(137, 1, "אם", "יש", "לך", "קציר", "אתה", "עושה", "יום", "טוב")} "if you have a harvest you make a festival"; {SP_(137, 1, "בין", "שיש", "לך", "קציר", "ובין", "שאין", "לך", "קציר")} "whether you have a harvest or have no harvest"): THE FEAST UNCONDITIONED ON THE HARVEST — Exodus 23:16\'s name read as a condition and refused (the kin\'s ledger exo_23): the compile\'s feast a calendar effect, no crop condition; "the feast of weeks" the Bible\'s two seats (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(137, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE MEASURE OF THE FREEWILL OFFERING OF YOUR HAND WHICH YOU GIVE" — IT TEACHES THAT A MAN BRINGS HIS OBLIGATION FROM UNCONSECRATED STOCK. ({SP_(137, 2, "מביא", "חובתו", "מן", "החלין")} "brings his obligation from the unconsecrated"): 129:6\'s rule again at the feast of weeks — the festival offering from one\'s own. Fresh.')
srow(137, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT IF HE WISHES TO BRING FROM THE TITHE HE MAY? THE TEACHING SAYS "AS THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS BLESSED YOU". ({SP_(137, 3, "להביא", "ממעשר", "יביא")} "to bring from the tithe, he may bring"): the cattle tithe admitted for the surplus (Mishnah Menachot 7:6; Chagigah 1:3 the exam — the English\'s note reads it otherwise). Fresh.')
srow(138, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REJOICE" (16:11) — REJOICING IS SAID HERE AND REJOICING IS SAID THERE (27:7): AS THE REJOICING SAID THERE IS PEACE OFFERINGS, SO HERE. The head row of piska 138 ({SP_(138, 1, "נאמרה", "כאן", "שמחה", "ונאמרה", "להלן", "שמחה")} "rejoicing is said here and rejoicing is said there"; {SP_(138, 1, "שלמים")} "peace offerings"): I2 (checked) ON THE WORD "REJOICE" WITH 27:7 (a verse ahead — never read ahead; the row recorded from its citation) — REJOICING IS AN OFFERING EATEN: the compile\'s joy effect the peace offering (Chagigah 8a the segment); the book\'s eight "rejoice" seats asserted. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12\'s sitting, deu_12_reeh).')
srow(138, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU AND YOUR SON AND YOUR DAUGHTER AND YOUR MANSERVANT AND YOUR MAIDSERVANT AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES AND THE SOJOURNER" — THE DEARER, THE DEARER FIRST. ({SP_(138, 2, "חביב", "חביב", "קודם")} "the dearer, the dearer first"): THE HOUSEHOLD LIST AS A PRECEDENCE — the nine members in order (16:11 = 16:14, asserted identical): the joy\'s distribution a ranked parameter (as the poor\'s ranks at 15:7). Fresh.')
srow(138, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAYS: THREE COMMANDMENTS HOLD ON THE PILGRIMAGE — THE FESTIVAL OFFERING, THE APPEARANCE, AND REJOICING. ({SP_(138, 3, "שלש", "מצוות", "נוהגות", "ברגל")} "three commandments hold on the pilgrimage"; {SP_(138, 3, "חגיגה", "ראיה", "ושמחה")} "the festival offering, the appearance and rejoicing"): THE PILGRIMAGE\'S THREE EFFECTS NAMED — chagigah, re\'iyah, simchah: the compile\'s three cells for each of the three feasts (Mishnah Chagigah 1 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(138, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'THE APPEARANCE HAS WHAT THE OTHER TWO LACK; THE FESTIVAL OFFERING WHAT THE OTHER TWO LACK; REJOICING WHAT THE OTHER TWO LACK. The row without a citation ({SP_(138, 4, "יש", "בראיה", "שאין", "בשתיהן")} "the appearance has what is not in the two"): the three distinguished. Fresh.')
srow(138, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE APPEARANCE — WHOLLY TO THE MOST HIGH, WHICH THE OTHER TWO LACK. ({SP_(138, 5, "ראיה", "כלה", "לגבוה")} "the appearance wholly to the Most High"): the appearance offering a burnt offering. Fresh.')
srow(138, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'THE FESTIVAL OFFERING — HOLDS BEFORE THE WORD AND AFTER THE WORD, WHICH THE OTHER TWO LACK. ({SP_(138, 6, "נוהגת", "לפני", "הדבר", "ולאחר", "הדבר")} "holds before the word and after the word"): the chagigah older than Sinai (Exodus 5:1 the English\'s pointer) — an installation fact for the tape (the feast offered before the law was given). Fresh.')
srow(138, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'REJOICING — HOLDS FOR MEN AND FOR WOMEN, WHICH THE OTHER TWO LACK. ({SP_(138, 7, "נוהגת", "באנשים", "ובנשים")} "holds for men and for women"): the joy\'s subjects both sexes; the appearance the males (143:3). Tosefta Chagigah 1:4. Fresh.')
srow(138, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'SINCE EACH HAS WHAT THE OTHER LACKS, SCRIPTURE HAD TO SAY THEM ALL. The row without a citation ({SP_(138, 8, "צרך", "הכתוב", "לומר", "את", "כלן")} "Scripture needed to say them all"): the three written because none is derivable from the others. Fresh.')
srow(139, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REMEMBER THAT YOU WERE A SLAVE IN EGYPT, AND KEEP AND DO THESE STATUTES" (16:12) — DOES IT TEACH THAT WHAT HOLDS AT THE ASSEMBLY HOLDS AT PASSOVER AND THE FEAST, OR EVEN THAT WHAT HOLDS AT PASSOVER AND THE FEAST HOLDS AT THE ASSEMBLY? "THESE" — THESE HOLD AT THE ASSEMBLY, BUT NOT THE BOOTH, THE PALM, THE SEVEN DAYS AND THE UNLEAVENED BREAD. The one row of piska 139 ({SP_(139, 1, "שכל", "שנוהגים", "בעצרת", "נוהגים", "בפסח", "וחג")} "that all that hold at the assembly hold at Passover and the feast"; {SP_(139, 1, "ואין", "סכה", "ולולב", "ושבעה", "ומצה", "נוהגים", "בעצרת")} "and the booth, the palm, the seven days and the unleavened bread do not hold at the assembly"): "THESE" THE LIMITING WORD — the feast of weeks\' one day carries the assembly\'s statutes and none of the other feasts\' rites: the compile\'s three feasts three cells, not one with flags; "remember that you were a slave" the book\'s five seats (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(140, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FEAST OF BOOTHS YOU SHALL MAKE FOR YOURSELF SEVEN DAYS" (16:13) — FOR THE COMMON MAN; WHENCE ALSO FOR THE MOST HIGH? "THE FEAST OF BOOTHS SEVEN DAYS TO THE LORD" (LEVITICUS 23:34). The head row of piska 140 ({SP_(140, 1, "להדיוט", "מנין", "אף", "לגבוה")} "for the common man; whence also for the Most High"): "for yourself" against "to the LORD" — the two verses\' two beneficiaries (the kin\'s ledger); "the feast of booths" spelled defective at 16:13 alone in the Bible (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(140, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'IF SO WHY "YOU SHALL MAKE FOR YOURSELF"? WHENEVER YOU MAKE A BOOTH, I ACCOUNT IT AS IF YOU MADE IT FOR THE MOST HIGH. ({SP_(140, 2, "מעלה", "אני", "עליך", "כאלו", "לגבוה", "אתה", "עושה")} "I account it to you as if you made it for the Most High"): the two beneficiaries one. Fresh.')
srow(140, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL MAKE FOR YOURSELF" — TO THE EXCLUSION OF AN OLD BOOTH. FROM HERE YOU SAY (MISHNAH SUKKAH 1:4): IF HE TRAINED A VINE, A GOURD OR IVY OVER IT AND ROOFED OVER THEM, IT IS DISQUALIFIED. ({SP_(140, 3, "פרט", "לסכה", "ישנה")} "to the exclusion of an old booth"; {SP_(140, 3, "וסיכך", "על", "גבן", "פסולה")} "and roofed over them — disqualified"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — "make" requires a making for the feast: the booth\'s validity cell (the roof made, not grown; the old booth a dispute the exam carries — Sukkah 9a the segment). Fresh.')
srow(140, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER SAYS: AS A MAN DOES NOT FULFIL HIS DUTY ON THE FIRST DAY WITH HIS FELLOW\'S PALM, SO NOT WITH HIS FELLOW\'S BOOTH — "YOU SHALL MAKE FOR YOURSELF". THE SAGES: WITH HIS FELLOW\'S PALM HE DOES NOT — "YOU SHALL TAKE FOR YOURSELVES" (LEVITICUS 23:40), EACH ONE; WITH HIS FELLOW\'S BOOTH HE DOES — "ALL THE NATIVE-BORN IN ISRAEL SHALL DWELL IN BOOTHS" (LEVITICUS 23:42), ALL ISRAEL IN ONE BOOTH. ({SP_(140, 4, "בסכתו", "של", "חברו")} "in his fellow\'s booth"; {SP_(140, 4, "כל", "ישראל", "ישבו", "בסכה", "אחת")} "all Israel shall dwell in one booth"): THE OWNERSHIP DISPUTE — the palm each man\'s, the booth shared (the sages) or each man\'s (R. Eliezer): Mishnah Sukkah 3 the exam; the compile\'s ownership parameter with two arms. Fresh.')
srow(140, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SIMEON SAYS: PASSOVER AND THE FEAST, WHICH ARE NOT SEASONS OF WORK — HE MADE THIS ONE SEVEN AND THAT ONE EIGHT; THE ASSEMBLY, A SEASON OF WORK, ONE DAY ONLY: SCRIPTURE SPARED ISRAEL. The row without a citation ({SP_(140, 5, "עשה", "זה", "שבעה", "וזה", "שמונה")} "He made this one seven and that one eight"; {SP_(140, 5, "שחסך", "הכתוב", "לישראל")} "that Scripture spared Israel"): THE THREE FEASTS\' LENGTHS 7 / 1 / 8 given a reason from the field\'s calendar — the compile\'s durations (the eighth day of booths counted in). Fresh.')
srow(140, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU GATHER IN FROM YOUR THRESHING-FLOOR AND YOUR WINEPRESS" — AS THE FLOOR AND THE PRESS ARE PARTICULAR IN GROWING ON THE PAST YEAR\'S WATER, VEGETABLES WENT OUT, WHICH DO NOT — R. YOSE THE GALILEAN\'S WORDS. ({SP_(140, 6, "שהם", "גדלים", "על", "מי", "שנה", "שעברה")} "that they grow on the past year\'s water"; {SP_(140, 6, "יצאו", "ירקות")} "vegetables went out"): the tithe-year of vegetables from the feast\'s gathering clause — a tithe parameter (Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1 / Sheviit 2 the exam). Fresh.')
srow(140, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA SAYS: AS THE FLOOR AND THE PRESS ARE PARTICULAR IN NOT GROWING ON ALL WATERS, THEREFORE TITHED BY THE PAST YEAR, VEGETABLES WENT OUT, WHICH GROW ON ALL WATERS, THEREFORE TITHED BY THE COMING YEAR. The row without a citation ({SP_(140, 7, "שאין", "גדלים", "על", "כל", "מים")} "that they do not grow on all waters"; {SP_(140, 7, "מתעשרים", "לשנה", "הבאה")} "tithed for the coming year"): the same rule by a different feature — a dispute in the reasoning, one verdict. Fresh.')
srow(141, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REJOICE" (16:14) — WITH EVERY KIND OF REJOICING. The head row of piska 141 ({SP_(141, 1, "בכל", "מיני", "שמחות")} "with every kind of rejoicing"): the joy\'s means widened. Fresh.')
srow(141, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN WITH BIRDS AND MEAL OFFERINGS? THE TEACHING SAYS "IN YOUR FEAST" — WITH THAT FROM WHICH THE FESTIVAL OFFERING COMES; BIRDS AND MEAL OFFERINGS WENT OUT. ({SP_(141, 2, "במה", "שחגיגה", "באה", "מהם")} "with that from which the festival offering comes"; {SP_(141, 2, "יצאו", "עופות", "ומנחות")} "birds and meal offerings went out"): the joy\'s offering flesh only (Mishnah Chagigah 1:4 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(141, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU AND YOUR SON AND YOUR DAUGHTER AND YOUR MANSERVANT AND YOUR MAIDSERVANT AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES" — THE DEARER, THE DEARER FIRST. ({SP_(141, 3, "חביב", "חביב", "קודם")} "the dearer, the dearer first"): 138:2 again at the feast of booths — the precedence holds at both lists. Fresh.')
srow(142, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEVEN DAYS YOU SHALL KEEP THE FEAST TO THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE" (16:15) — IS IT NOT ALREADY SAID "THE FEAST OF BOOTHS SEVEN DAYS TO THE LORD" (LEVITICUS 23:34)? WHY "SEVEN DAYS"? IT TEACHES THAT THE WHOLE PILGRIMAGE COMPENSATES FOR THE FIRST DAY. The head row of piska 142 ({SP_(142, 1, "שכל", "הרגל", "תשלומים", "לראשון")} "that the whole pilgrimage is compensation for the first"): THE SEVEN DAYS AS A WINDOW — the festival offering missed on the first day brought any day of the seven (Mishnah Chagigah 1:6 the exam): the compile\'s window parameter. Fresh.')
srow(142, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'[MIGHT THE FESTIVAL OFFERING BE REQUIRED ALL SEVEN? "IT" (LEVITICUS 23:41).] IF SO WHY "SEVEN DAYS"? COMPENSATION ALL SEVEN. ({SP_(142, 2, "תשלומים", "כל", "שבעה")} "compensation all seven"): the bracketed question (the English\'s note — a scribe\'s doubling) and the answer: one offering, seven days to bring it. Fresh.')
srow(142, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL BLESS YOU" — MIGHT IT BE IN THAT KIND ALONE? THE TEACHING SAYS "IN ALL YOUR PRODUCE AND IN ALL THE WORK OF YOUR HANDS". ({SP_(142, 3, "יכול", "בו", "במין")} "might it be in that kind"; {SP_(142, 3, "בכל", "תבואתך", "ובכל", "מעשה", "ידיך")} "in all your produce and in all the work of your hands"): the blessing\'s scope all crops. Fresh.')
srow(142, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL BE ALTOGETHER JOYFUL" — TO INCLUDE THE NIGHT OF THE FIRST FESTIVAL DAY FOR REJOICING. ({SP_(142, 4, "לרבות", "לילי", "יום", "טוב", "הראשון", "לשמחה")} "to include the nights of the first festival day for rejoicing"): the joy\'s first night in. Fresh.')
srow(142, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT I INCLUDE THE NIGHT OF THE LAST FESTIVAL DAY? THE TEACHING SAYS "ONLY". ({SP_(142, 5, "לילי", "יום", "טוב", "האחרון")} "the nights of the last festival day"): "ONLY" THE LIMITING WORD — the last night out (the offering cannot be slaughtered at night after the feast): the joy window\'s two edges from "altogether" and "only" (Sukkah 48a the segment). Fresh.')
srow(142, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH CHAGIGAH 1:4): ISRAEL FULFIL THEIR DUTY WITH VOWS AND FREEWILL OFFERINGS. MIGHT IT BE EVEN WITH BIRDS AND MEAL OFFERINGS? "ONLY". ({SP_(142, 6, "יוצאים", "ידי", "חובתם", "בנדרים", "ובנדבות")} "fulfil their duty with vows and freewill offerings"): the Mishnah cited in the Hebrew itself — vowed animals serve the joy; 141:2\'s exclusion again. Fresh.')
print('the Sifrei rows 137-142 typed:', len(S), '| the cuts\' misses:', FAIL)
